1
00:00:07,480 --> 00:00:08,310
My...

2
00:00:08,393 --> 00:00:10,517
my strength, it's... it's gone. I...

3
00:00:10,600 --> 00:00:12,377
I can't lift...

4
00:00:12,460 --> 00:00:13,377
Miseria.

5
00:00:13,460 --> 00:00:15,620
Even my vision's blurry. Dammit.

6
00:00:15,980 --> 00:00:16,997
Is this it?

7
00:00:17,080 --> 00:00:18,920
I knew this moment would come.

8
00:00:19,220 --> 00:00:20,417
But why now?

9
00:00:20,500 --> 00:00:22,080
I must press on.

10
00:00:23,700 --> 00:00:24,597
Huh? What did...

11
00:00:24,680 --> 00:00:25,537
Wait, that's right.

12
00:00:25,620 --> 00:00:29,017
Bucciarati and his crew are
trying to get somewhere right now.

13
00:00:29,100 --> 00:00:31,394
This could be my chance to learn where.

14
00:00:31,740 --> 00:00:34,152
I know the boss is desperate to find out.

15
00:00:35,980 --> 00:00:38,333
Um, uh, looks like you could use a hand.

16
00:00:38,580 --> 00:00:41,260
Here, I'm happy to
assist you if you'd like.

17
00:00:42,280 --> 00:00:43,110
You again?

18
00:00:43,420 --> 00:00:44,773
Why are you still here?

19
00:00:45,180 --> 00:00:46,140
I'll be fine.

20
00:00:46,580 --> 00:00:48,051
You should get to safety.

21
00:00:48,960 --> 00:00:49,790
I'm sorry.

22
00:00:49,873 --> 00:00:51,777
I don't want to seem pushy or anything.

23
00:00:51,860 --> 00:00:54,625
I just want to make sure
you get across safely.

24
00:00:55,100 --> 00:00:57,629
It would put me at ease
if you let me help.

25
00:00:59,800 --> 00:01:02,780
I mean, um, only if you don't mind.

26
00:01:04,400 --> 00:01:08,280
On second thought, I suppose
I could use a touch of help.

27
00:01:10,240 --> 00:01:12,017
Where are we heading, good sir?

28
00:01:12,100 --> 00:01:13,000
Not too far.

29
00:01:13,320 --> 00:01:15,540
Just the entrance to the Coliseum.

30
00:01:17,740 --> 00:01:20,093
So that's where you're trying to get to.

31
00:02:11,520 --> 00:02:12,350
Thank you

32
00:02:12,433 --> 00:02:19,280
so

33
00:02:23,620 --> 00:02:28,120
much for watching.

34
00:02:30,820 --> 00:02:33,517
Don't care, don't care
You hear it, don't you?

35
00:02:33,600 --> 00:02:34,430
You hear it, don't you?

36
00:02:34,513 --> 00:02:39,317
When your body dies,
I'll be here to help you?

37
00:02:39,400 --> 00:02:40,300
Hell, no!

38
00:02:40,680 --> 00:02:45,420
It's the beginning of the doorbell ring

39
00:02:58,620 --> 00:02:59,480
Watch out!

40
00:03:01,500 --> 00:03:02,680
Hey, are you okay?

41
00:03:02,920 --> 00:03:05,626
You gotta look both ways
when you're cr - Huh?

42
00:03:05,780 --> 00:03:06,610
What the?

43
00:03:06,740 --> 00:03:08,940
His hands are so cold and clammy.

44
00:03:09,600 --> 00:03:10,460
I'm sorry.

45
00:03:11,260 --> 00:03:13,120
This thing I just tripped on.

46
00:03:13,480 --> 00:03:14,800
Is it a guardrail?

47
00:03:18,620 --> 00:03:19,900
Hold on a second.

48
00:03:20,580 --> 00:03:22,698
Does this mean he can't see anymore?

49
00:03:22,940 --> 00:03:26,411
And he didn't even flinch when
that driver honked his horn.

50
00:03:26,620 --> 00:03:28,260
Are his ears busted too?

51
00:03:34,100 --> 00:03:36,041
That gas you have on your throat.

52
00:03:36,260 --> 00:03:37,090
Did I...

53
00:03:37,173 --> 00:03:39,728
Did I do that to you
in the scuffle earlier?

54
00:03:40,360 --> 00:03:42,660
No, that's probably not the case.

55
00:03:42,900 --> 00:03:44,777
The wound has already stopped bleeding.

56
00:03:44,860 --> 00:03:46,200
That means it's older.

57
00:03:46,840 --> 00:03:48,937
How'd you manage to hurt yourself there?

58
00:03:49,020 --> 00:03:50,377
He's staring right at it.

59
00:03:50,460 --> 00:03:52,060
So he can't still see?

60
00:03:52,400 --> 00:03:54,437
Wait, but it's hidden under my collar.

61
00:03:54,520 --> 00:03:56,991
Or the injury I got from fighting Risotto.

62
00:03:58,100 --> 00:04:02,520
How kind of you to help me pick that
up. Crazy mille. I'll take that.

63
00:04:04,220 --> 00:04:06,260
Now then, let's get going.

64
00:04:12,100 --> 00:04:13,360
Well, all right.

65
00:04:14,120 --> 00:04:15,440
So he can hear me.

66
00:04:15,980 --> 00:04:20,500
Still, whatever's ailing him seems way
more complex than just battle wounds.

67
00:04:21,140 --> 00:04:23,080
What's making him act like this?

68
00:04:29,400 --> 00:04:30,230
Oh, shit.

69
00:04:30,520 --> 00:04:32,420
It's Guido Mista. Figures.

70
00:04:32,620 --> 00:04:34,477
I knew things were going too well.

71
00:04:34,560 --> 00:04:37,517
Should have guessed his friends
wouldn't be too far behind.

72
00:04:37,600 --> 00:04:38,430
Is something the matter?

73
00:04:38,513 --> 00:04:39,343
What's wrong?

74
00:04:39,426 --> 00:04:40,857
We've yet to finish crossing.

75
00:04:40,940 --> 00:04:42,497
I'm sorry. It's just...

76
00:04:42,580 --> 00:04:43,840
I need to sit down.

77
00:04:44,080 --> 00:04:45,198
My wound opened up.

78
00:04:45,300 --> 00:04:47,124
I'll just be a minute, I swear.

79
00:04:49,040 --> 00:04:50,180
Crap, crap, crap!

80
00:04:50,300 --> 00:04:51,130
He's coming!

81
00:04:51,620 --> 00:04:54,267
Excuse my bluntness,
but I need to get going.

82
00:04:54,520 --> 00:04:56,237
Thank you for all the help
you've given me so far.

83
00:04:56,320 --> 00:04:57,150
No, not now!

84
00:04:57,240 --> 00:04:58,652
I need you to stay here!

85
00:04:59,820 --> 00:05:02,060
I mean, there's another car coming.

86
00:05:02,440 --> 00:05:04,157
We can keep crossing once it passes.

87
00:05:04,240 --> 00:05:05,070
It's fine.

88
00:05:05,153 --> 00:05:06,737
We've already cleared
that side of the road.

89
00:05:06,820 --> 00:05:08,437
It should be safe to continue.

90
00:05:08,520 --> 00:05:10,226
Come on, the clock's ticking.

91
00:05:11,020 --> 00:05:13,240
Damn it! No! Mista's coming!

92
00:05:13,660 --> 00:05:17,300
I'll just have to kill
him! Right here! Right now!

93
00:05:22,760 --> 00:05:26,113
Oh my goodness, I wonder what
that noise could have been.

94
00:05:29,940 --> 00:05:31,540
For God's sake, what now?

95
00:05:31,800 --> 00:05:33,976
What perplexing game are you playing?

96
00:05:37,760 --> 00:05:40,017
Why do you have to call now of all times?

97
00:05:40,100 --> 00:05:41,747
Do you want him to find out?

98
00:05:42,060 --> 00:05:43,020
Wait a second.

99
00:05:44,780 --> 00:05:46,839
Would you quit blowing me up, dude?

100
00:05:46,980 --> 00:05:49,277
What's so damn important, you
gotta tell me right this second.

101
00:05:49,360 --> 00:05:51,478
You're gonna blow my freaking cover.

102
00:05:54,420 --> 00:05:56,420
Trish, get back inside the turtle.

103
00:05:56,820 --> 00:05:58,644
We're not out of the woods yet.

104
00:05:58,780 --> 00:06:00,604
Please keep a low head for now.

105
00:06:00,760 --> 00:06:01,590
No, wait.

106
00:06:01,673 --> 00:06:02,521
We're not alone.

107
00:06:02,620 --> 00:06:03,561
I can sense him.

108
00:06:04,200 --> 00:06:05,729
He's here, I'm sure of it.

109
00:06:06,020 --> 00:06:07,314
That horrible feeling.

110
00:06:08,080 --> 00:06:09,277
There's no mistaking it.

111
00:06:09,360 --> 00:06:10,419
It's the same one.

112
00:06:11,820 --> 00:06:12,650
Wait.

113
00:06:13,020 --> 00:06:13,850
I know you.

114
00:06:16,860 --> 00:06:18,980
I finally recognize you.

115
00:06:22,260 --> 00:06:23,090
You're…

116
00:06:26,360 --> 00:06:27,190
Trish!

117
00:06:28,280 --> 00:06:30,200
I feel it. He's nearby.

118
00:06:30,660 --> 00:06:32,560
The boss is closing in on us.

119
00:06:32,820 --> 00:06:34,197
Tell me which way to shoot.

120
00:06:34,280 --> 00:06:35,937
Can you tell us exactly where he is?

121
00:06:36,020 --> 00:06:38,902
He suddenly appeared, but
I can't pinpoint where.

122
00:06:39,420 --> 00:06:40,250
You're safe.

123
00:06:40,420 --> 00:06:41,832
Thank the heavens above.

124
00:06:42,480 --> 00:06:43,660
Excellent work.

125
00:06:43,920 --> 00:06:45,857
You've achieved an incredible feat,

126
00:06:45,940 --> 00:06:49,175
although I expect nothing
short of perfection from you.

127
00:06:49,480 --> 00:06:50,320
Rest assured.

128
00:06:50,780 --> 00:06:53,368
Bujarati's eyes may
seem to be fixed on you?

129
00:06:53,500 --> 00:06:55,700
but he does not truly see you.

130
00:06:58,400 --> 00:06:59,400
Wait, what?

131
00:06:59,660 --> 00:07:00,760
I don't get it.

132
00:07:01,160 --> 00:07:05,860
I possess no insight as to how,
but he's now a reanimated corpse.

133
00:07:06,580 --> 00:07:10,140
He lacks both a pulse and a
working respiratory system.

134
00:07:10,680 --> 00:07:15,445
He's lost use of his eyes, and his eardrums
were ruptured in his fight with Seko.

135
00:07:15,740 --> 00:07:20,180
The only thing he's able to see,
Deep, is a rough outline of your soul.

136
00:07:20,460 --> 00:07:23,166
The only sound he can
hear are its vibrations.

137
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:26,540
Physical objects are now invisible to him.

138
00:07:26,780 --> 00:07:30,192
He sees not the car, but the
essence of the driver within.

139
00:07:30,580 --> 00:07:31,720
Trish, talk to me.

140
00:07:32,000 --> 00:07:33,477
Did something happen to you?

141
00:07:33,560 --> 00:07:37,737
It just so happens my daughter
and I am at near-identical auras.

142
00:07:37,820 --> 00:07:40,920
And for the moment, I
have cloaked you in mine.

143
00:07:41,820 --> 00:07:44,777
Bucciarati presently believes
he is looking at Trish.

144
00:07:44,860 --> 00:07:46,742
You must maintain this illusion.

145
00:07:46,860 --> 00:07:51,331
Let him be your personal guide and have
him take you to this secret meeting.

146
00:07:51,820 --> 00:07:52,650
Trish.

147
00:07:53,280 --> 00:07:54,380
I'm so sorry.

148
00:07:54,620 --> 00:07:56,297
I think I got a little lightheaded.

149
00:07:56,380 --> 00:07:57,498
But thank goodness.

150
00:07:57,700 --> 00:07:59,582
I'm relieved to see you're okay.

151
00:07:59,880 --> 00:08:01,140
Yeah, I am.

152
00:08:01,480 --> 00:08:04,245
By the way, have you seen
a young man anywhere?

153
00:08:04,480 --> 00:08:05,477
Oh yeah, I think so.

154
00:08:05,560 --> 00:08:08,397
He looked kind of flustered
and left in a big hurry.

155
00:08:08,480 --> 00:08:10,437
We shouldn't worry about him, though.

156
00:08:10,520 --> 00:08:12,777
Right now, we need to
stay focused on moving.

157
00:08:12,860 --> 00:08:13,690
You're right.

158
00:08:14,160 --> 00:08:16,380
I'm sorry, but could...

159
00:08:17,020 --> 00:08:19,373
Could you give me a little hand, please?

160
00:08:19,900 --> 00:08:20,730
Yes.

161
00:08:21,200 --> 00:08:22,300
I'd be glad to.

162
00:08:33,240 --> 00:08:35,060
In the outskirts of Napoli.

163
00:08:37,220 --> 00:08:38,050
I...

164
00:08:38,133 --> 00:08:38,980
I have a house.

165
00:08:39,280 --> 00:08:45,160
It isn't big, but when this is all over,
by chance you find yourself needing a home,

166
00:08:45,420 --> 00:08:47,420
you'll be more than welcome there.

167
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:56,420
You know, the area's pretty nice.

168
00:08:56,680 --> 00:08:57,817
Good eats and everything.

169
00:08:57,900 --> 00:08:59,620
And it's close to the beach.

170
00:09:00,300 --> 00:09:02,777
I know this has all
been one big nightmare,

171
00:09:02,860 --> 00:09:06,080
but I promise a much
brighter future is waiting.

172
00:09:07,320 --> 00:09:09,940
Sounds nice, but let's stay focused.

173
00:09:10,260 --> 00:09:12,217
Which way do you want me to steer us next?

174
00:09:12,300 --> 00:09:14,535
The stairs, please, if you don't mind.

175
00:09:14,700 --> 00:09:15,582
You mean these?

176
00:09:15,680 --> 00:09:17,260
Do not turn around, Dobio!

177
00:09:17,560 --> 00:09:18,720
Just keep going!

178
00:09:19,080 --> 00:09:21,237
Continue onward as if nothing happened.

179
00:09:21,320 --> 00:09:22,202
Someone's here.

180
00:09:22,800 --> 00:09:26,800
Behind the stone pillars above,
someone is watching your every move.

181
00:09:27,400 --> 00:09:30,720
So, he really is here to
rendezvous with our foes.

182
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:32,300
But who could they be?

183
00:09:32,620 --> 00:09:34,444
I've zero intel on this person.

184
00:09:34,880 --> 00:09:37,857
How are you so sure that
they're really here, boss?

185
00:09:37,940 --> 00:09:39,497
I mean, even if you're right,

186
00:09:39,580 --> 00:09:42,937
how am I supposed to figure out who
they are if I can't turn around?

187
00:09:43,020 --> 00:09:44,720
Look into Butorati's eyes.

188
00:09:44,920 --> 00:09:45,897
They will tell you.

189
00:09:45,980 --> 00:09:48,098
Quick, while the reflection's there!

190
00:09:48,560 --> 00:09:49,390
Don't move.

191
00:09:49,660 --> 00:09:51,131
Stay right where you are.

192
00:09:51,600 --> 00:09:55,776
Get a step closer to those stairs,
and our agreement will be nullified.

193
00:09:57,820 --> 00:09:59,277
You were right. Crap.

194
00:09:59,360 --> 00:10:01,037
Someone's hiding out behind the pillar.

195
00:10:01,120 --> 00:10:01,950
I saw him.

196
00:10:02,140 --> 00:10:04,220
My name is Bruno Bucciarati.

197
00:10:04,540 --> 00:10:07,717
I've come here on your promise
to reveal the boss's weakness.

198
00:10:07,800 --> 00:10:09,617
I hope you mean to keep your word.

199
00:10:09,700 --> 00:10:10,720
You, I know.

200
00:10:11,000 --> 00:10:12,397
The problem's your friend.

201
00:10:12,480 --> 00:10:14,577
I never said you could bring a plus one.

202
00:10:14,660 --> 00:10:17,597
I can't find a shred of
data on them in my records.

203
00:10:17,680 --> 00:10:19,033
Of course you wouldn't.

204
00:10:19,160 --> 00:10:21,217
Trish here isn't a member of the Family.

205
00:10:21,300 --> 00:10:24,124
In fact, we met barely
more than a few days ago.

206
00:10:24,660 --> 00:10:27,542
But as you can clearly
see, she's batting for us.

207
00:10:28,800 --> 00:10:29,700
Trish, you say?

208
00:10:29,980 --> 00:10:32,274
To my knowledge, that's a woman's name.

209
00:10:32,500 --> 00:10:33,380
Your point?

210
00:10:34,020 --> 00:10:37,140
Merida, I think the jig's
up, boss. Calm down.

211
00:10:37,500 --> 00:10:38,971
Listen, you must respond.

212
00:10:39,760 --> 00:10:42,397
Act furious at him for
doubting your femininity.

213
00:10:42,480 --> 00:10:43,310
Do it, Deep.

214
00:10:44,860 --> 00:10:48,331
You got some kind of problem
with me being a girl, you pig?

215
00:10:51,800 --> 00:10:54,017
My deepest apologies, mademoiselle.

216
00:10:54,100 --> 00:10:56,380
I can't see very well in this light.

217
00:10:57,340 --> 00:10:59,257
Is the lady a stand user?

218
00:10:59,340 --> 00:11:00,857
Yes, she is.

219
00:11:00,940 --> 00:11:02,157
Now down to business.

220
00:11:02,240 --> 00:11:04,497
I think it's about time
you tell us who you are.

221
00:11:04,580 --> 00:11:06,637
Let's talk about why you dragged me here.

222
00:11:06,720 --> 00:11:07,550
No, not yet.

223
00:11:07,633 --> 00:11:09,400
I'd like to see her stand first.

224
00:11:10,180 --> 00:11:11,157
And Trish.

225
00:11:11,240 --> 00:11:12,637
No sudden movements.

226
00:11:12,720 --> 00:11:14,537
I have no data on you.

227
00:11:14,620 --> 00:11:19,500
But show me your stand and I'll get
over it. Shit! What now? Damn it.

228
00:11:19,700 --> 00:11:22,697
It appears we're dealing
with a seasoned gladiator.

229
00:11:22,780 --> 00:11:25,839
He's even trying to gauge
a potential enemy's range.

230
00:11:26,300 --> 00:11:27,820
Who is this man?

231
00:11:27,960 --> 00:11:29,357
How have I never heard of him?

232
00:11:29,440 --> 00:11:30,440
What's wrong now?

233
00:11:30,740 --> 00:11:32,034
Shouldn't be too hard.

234
00:11:32,360 --> 00:11:35,478
Think of it like lifting up
your skirt nice and slow.

235
00:11:36,720 --> 00:11:37,980
That's... But how?

236
00:11:38,220 --> 00:11:39,740
How does he possess that?

237
00:11:40,500 --> 00:11:41,537
That arrow...

238
00:11:41,620 --> 00:11:42,700
There's no doubt.

239
00:11:42,980 --> 00:11:44,360
It's the same artifact.

240
00:11:45,620 --> 00:11:48,300
And that bloodlust, it's overwhelming.

241
00:11:48,700 --> 00:11:51,617
It almost feels like a
dagger racing for my heart.

242
00:11:51,700 --> 00:11:53,620
Where have I felt this before?

243
00:11:55,080 --> 00:11:55,960
Mon Dieu!

244
00:11:56,800 --> 00:11:58,680
Wait, that's right.

245
00:11:58,940 --> 00:12:01,160
I have crossed paths with this man.

246
00:12:01,460 --> 00:12:04,420
He utilized the arrow to
track me down back then.

247
00:12:05,100 --> 00:12:06,300
I remember!

248
00:12:09,580 --> 00:12:14,600
In Egypt, I unearthed a scattering of
arrows was capable of awakening stands.

249
00:12:16,100 --> 00:12:21,180
I knew simply from beholding them, they
possessed a certain entrancing energy.

250
00:12:21,560 --> 00:12:25,320
An old woman by the name of
Nyaba, who had two right hands,

251
00:12:25,620 --> 00:12:28,973
asked that I sell her some in
exchange for their secrets.

252
00:12:29,520 --> 00:12:35,560
In truth, I only needed one, so I sold her
the other five for a very generous sum.

253
00:12:37,620 --> 00:12:41,740
That is when the old bag uttered
something I found truly bizarre.

254
00:12:44,100 --> 00:12:49,160
The arrow chooses people, and those
chosen are bound by a curious force.

255
00:12:49,500 --> 00:12:54,380
The 20th century was in its final
decade, and Dio had passed. At the time,

256
00:12:54,500 --> 00:12:56,377
my old friend Jotaro Kujo and I were

257
00:12:56,460 --> 00:12:59,342
investigating the arrow
which could awaken Stans.

258
00:13:00,640 --> 00:13:03,934
Word had reached us of a young
boy who had pilfered them

259
00:13:04,060 --> 00:13:07,240
so he split up and scoured
the globe for the bastard.

260
00:13:07,980 --> 00:13:10,160
Jotaro would search America and Asia,

261
00:13:10,920 --> 00:13:16,140
And I, Europe and Africa, I soon managed
to learn the arrow was somewhere in Italy,

262
00:13:16,460 --> 00:13:19,989
hidden in a region suddenly
overcome by drug-related crimes.

263
00:13:22,960 --> 00:13:26,057
I focused my search on
a specific region where

264
00:13:26,140 --> 00:13:29,060
juvenile drug deaths had
seen an unusual jump.

265
00:13:29,560 --> 00:13:31,972
That's when I knew we were getting close.

266
00:13:33,800 --> 00:13:34,630
However...

267
00:13:37,120 --> 00:13:41,080
In a few years, my syndicate
was on the cusp of perfection.

268
00:13:41,520 --> 00:13:43,800
My Family swore allegiance to me.

269
00:13:44,160 --> 00:13:46,800
I had men in every crevice of society.

270
00:13:47,560 --> 00:13:52,380
Then I discovered that someone was
plotting to unveil my identity.

271
00:13:56,000 --> 00:13:58,880
In the end, I'd finish them off myself.

272
00:13:59,280 --> 00:14:00,720
It was the only way.

273
00:14:01,240 --> 00:14:03,060
I'd made my decision.

274
00:14:04,440 --> 00:14:07,277
Ultimately I committed two fatal errors.

275
00:14:07,360 --> 00:14:09,577
First was my failure to recognize this

276
00:14:09,660 --> 00:14:12,425
syndicate had already
matured to full strength.

277
00:14:13,660 --> 00:14:18,757
Communications, the government, the
press, society had me completely isolated.

278
00:14:18,840 --> 00:14:22,120
Then came my second and grievous mistake.

279
00:14:22,820 --> 00:14:24,480
Silver chariot.

280
00:14:26,500 --> 00:14:28,217
Since you're about to die,

281
00:14:28,300 --> 00:14:31,277
I might as well tell you
the man who would unearth

282
00:14:31,360 --> 00:14:34,301
those arrows he possessed
a power many times more.

283
00:14:34,440 --> 00:14:36,080
than I could ever imagine!

284
00:14:36,500 --> 00:14:39,060
Long before your gaze
can hope to reach me!

285
00:14:41,820 --> 00:14:45,080
His ability breaks time!

286
00:14:45,420 --> 00:14:47,620
You'll have already left this world!

287
00:14:54,960 --> 00:14:56,237
Has hope...

288
00:14:56,320 --> 00:14:58,100
Perished from the Earth, too?

289
00:15:04,520 --> 00:15:06,980
I was certain I'd finish the job,

290
00:15:07,220 --> 00:15:09,597
to think one of them
would return from death,

291
00:15:09,680 --> 00:15:12,209
and with the arrow in
their grasp, no less.

292
00:15:12,700 --> 00:15:15,112
Butcherati, that man's no friend of ours.

293
00:15:16,240 --> 00:15:17,070
What?

294
00:15:17,500 --> 00:15:20,440
Butcherati, that bastard,
where'd he run off to?

295
00:15:22,020 --> 00:15:22,920
He's gone.

296
00:15:23,940 --> 00:15:28,540
Putan, where did he go, that little
uninvited guest of yours, where is he?

297
00:15:30,420 --> 00:15:31,250
Datrice...

298
00:15:31,333 --> 00:15:34,999
Answer me, dammit, where the hell
is that swine you brought with you?

299
00:15:44,240 --> 00:15:48,475
Nothing seemed to fall, but somehow
the broken piece found its way here.

300
00:15:48,920 --> 00:15:51,000
It couldn't be these movements.

301
00:15:53,060 --> 00:15:53,940
Did you see?

302
00:15:54,140 --> 00:15:55,375
Time to skip forward.

303
00:15:55,480 --> 00:15:57,097
Just like what happened in Venice.

304
00:15:57,180 --> 00:15:59,768
We climbed the stairs
before we realized it.

305
00:16:00,940 --> 00:16:02,120
We won't make it.

306
00:16:02,300 --> 00:16:04,200
He's already there. The boss.

307
00:16:04,440 --> 00:16:06,440
He's got our guy within his range!

308
00:16:25,820 --> 00:16:27,440
I'm being tested.

309
00:16:32,340 --> 00:16:36,680
In a moment, we will find out if
I'm prepared to vanquish my past.

310
00:16:36,960 --> 00:16:42,260
We really only grow once we've conquered
our phantoms, wouldn't you say?

311
00:16:45,520 --> 00:16:50,240
How lovely to see you again,
Jean-Pierre Polnareff.

312
00:16:50,540 --> 00:16:51,740
I know you!

313
00:16:55,660 --> 00:16:56,490
Diavolo!

314
00:16:58,440 --> 00:17:01,381
Fascinating how the past
can wriggle its way back,

315
00:17:01,560 --> 00:17:04,560
no matter how many pieces
I might cut it up into.

316
00:17:05,260 --> 00:17:09,517
You amaze me, I never thought I'd deal
with the same vermin more than once.

317
00:17:09,600 --> 00:17:11,017
How did you slither up here?

318
00:17:11,100 --> 00:17:12,629
Let me be perfectly clear.

319
00:17:12,780 --> 00:17:15,197
I couldn't care less
about how you managed to

320
00:17:15,280 --> 00:17:18,104
live after I slung you
like chum into the abyss.

321
00:17:18,720 --> 00:17:20,840
What interests me, Polnareff,

322
00:17:20,980 --> 00:17:22,937
is whatever little secret you were all so

323
00:17:23,020 --> 00:17:25,117
eager to share with
Butcherati and his men!

324
00:17:25,200 --> 00:17:27,837
Walk up those steps and
see what happens, asshole!

325
00:17:27,920 --> 00:17:30,617
I have the high ground while
you're stuck way down there!

326
00:17:30,700 --> 00:17:32,737
Why do you shrink from battling me?

327
00:17:32,820 --> 00:17:34,160
Do I scare you?

328
00:17:34,520 --> 00:17:36,814
Has your spirit lost some of its vigor?

329
00:17:36,980 --> 00:17:39,320
Or has your body now given in to time?

330
00:17:39,720 --> 00:17:41,896
What are you plotting with the arrow?

331
00:17:42,240 --> 00:17:43,460
This is impossible!

332
00:17:43,880 --> 00:17:46,174
I'm sure it was a kid I saw down there!

333
00:17:46,700 --> 00:17:47,759
Malodorous wretch!

334
00:17:48,040 --> 00:17:49,981
When did you get so close to me?!

335
00:17:50,500 --> 00:17:52,880
The high ground is mine! En Card!

336
00:17:53,160 --> 00:17:54,877
Say your goodbyes to that arrow!

337
00:17:54,960 --> 00:17:59,784
Once I've sent you back to the depths of
hell, you'll have no further need for it!

338
00:18:01,300 --> 00:18:02,130
There!

339
00:18:02,213 --> 00:18:03,220
Silver Terunosu!

340
00:18:05,520 --> 00:18:07,440
Still sharp as ever, I see.

341
00:18:07,660 --> 00:18:09,440
You in that stand of yours.

342
00:18:10,340 --> 00:18:12,575
Seems you've learned a new trick, too.

343
00:18:12,960 --> 00:18:15,017
You're trying to pinpoint
the moments I skip

344
00:18:15,100 --> 00:18:17,982
through time by keeping
count of the blood drops.

345
00:18:18,740 --> 00:18:19,570
Resourceful.

346
00:18:19,653 --> 00:18:21,655
A moment's difference reveals so much.

347
00:18:24,180 --> 00:18:26,517
Your grasp of time is masterful.

348
00:18:26,600 --> 00:18:31,237
Had I gone just a little bit closer, you
might have dealt a consequential blow.

349
00:18:31,320 --> 00:18:33,037
Unbelievable!

350
00:18:33,120 --> 00:18:36,477
How did Diablo reach the
Colosseum before the others?

351
00:18:36,560 --> 00:18:38,117
This is it.

352
00:18:38,200 --> 00:18:39,657
It's now or never.

353
00:18:39,740 --> 00:18:43,417
Whatever it takes, I have to
keep the flames of hope alive.

354
00:18:43,500 --> 00:18:46,917
You died the second you were in range.

355
00:18:47,000 --> 00:18:50,360
I'll I'll make sure you stay
that way, Emperor Crimson!

356
00:18:58,700 --> 00:19:02,477
When the sands of time resume,
you'll no longer be able to look?

357
00:19:02,560 --> 00:19:04,877
at your precious blood drops for guidance.

358
00:19:04,960 --> 00:19:06,880
A cursed mistake from my past.

359
00:19:07,120 --> 00:19:10,520
Behold, I shall obliterate you now! Die!

360
00:19:10,860 --> 00:19:13,300
Enjoy the fatal relief that time will...

361
00:19:14,680 --> 00:19:15,680
What's happening?

362
00:19:19,080 --> 00:19:21,157
The arrow! The stand!

363
00:19:21,240 --> 00:19:24,100
This nonsense will cease! Perish!

364
00:19:27,180 --> 00:19:28,680
This radiance!

365
00:19:28,860 --> 00:19:30,857
What's happening to Silver Chariot?

366
00:19:30,940 --> 00:19:32,140
Such sheer power!

367
00:19:32,440 --> 00:19:34,057
The arrow's bursting with it!

368
00:19:34,140 --> 00:19:35,000
This ends now!

369
00:19:35,240 --> 00:19:36,534
Time resume your flow!

370
00:19:41,620 --> 00:19:43,320
French rat, what now?

371
00:19:43,660 --> 00:19:48,542
No, don't tell me, is the arrow able to do
more than draw out the power of a stand?

372
00:19:48,860 --> 00:19:52,977
It's a long shot, but there's no other
way of keeping the arrow from him.

373
00:19:53,060 --> 00:19:55,117
It pains me that I had to show him.

374
00:19:55,200 --> 00:19:59,906
However, I can no longer deny I've lost
the strength to fully control the arrow.

375
00:20:00,440 --> 00:20:01,560
You can't run!

376
00:20:10,280 --> 00:20:13,380
The arrow is hope-given form.

377
00:20:14,000 --> 00:20:19,160
Whosoever comes to control it will
be able to control the world as well.

378
00:20:21,240 --> 00:20:22,070
Huh?

379
00:20:22,153 --> 00:20:23,440
It just happened again.

380
00:20:23,840 --> 00:20:24,781
Did you feel it?

381
00:20:24,880 --> 00:20:26,351
There was a blip in time.

382
00:20:26,660 --> 00:20:28,660
Trish, where'd you sense the boss?

383
00:20:30,220 --> 00:20:34,320
All those wasted years trying to
uncover the mystery of the arrow.

384
00:20:34,580 --> 00:20:36,698
I'm surprised you made it this long.

385
00:20:38,500 --> 00:20:40,420
What an utter travesty!

386
00:20:40,620 --> 00:20:42,420
The arrow is mine, you fool!

387
00:20:57,100 --> 00:21:00,200
Your valiant heart has
stopped beating at last.

388
00:21:00,420 --> 00:21:04,660
If it offers you any solace, know
that you did not die in vain.

389
00:21:05,200 --> 00:21:07,300
Fine, dear Jean-Bierre Polnareff.

390
00:21:07,880 --> 00:21:10,937
You've done me a greater service
than you'll ever realize.

391
00:21:11,020 --> 00:21:12,549
I tell you that sincerely.

392
00:21:13,560 --> 00:21:14,390
Giorno!

393
00:21:14,800 --> 00:21:18,240
I found Bucciarati! He's
right there! Come on! Shit!

394
00:21:18,480 --> 00:21:21,660
Poor guy got pummeled hard!
Bucciarati! Be careful!

395
00:21:21,940 --> 00:21:23,999
The boss is lurking somewhere near!

396
00:21:25,140 --> 00:21:25,970
You've come.

397
00:21:34,660 --> 00:21:35,490
What?

398
00:21:47,820 --> 00:21:49,900
Stop now! Who are you?

399
00:21:50,440 --> 00:21:52,205
Identify yourself immediately!

400
00:22:04,660 --> 00:22:08,520
What is just fiction or what is the truth?

401
00:22:09,480 --> 00:22:12,517
They have a mission, they have a passion.

402
00:22:12,600 --> 00:22:16,820
But they dare to tell us
what's bad and what's good!

403
00:22:17,840 --> 00:22:20,237
Stand up, join us.

404
00:22:20,320 --> 00:22:23,877
Come on, I'll say this a lie.

405
00:22:23,960 --> 00:22:28,277
We are the power, who'll be the future!

406
00:22:28,360 --> 00:22:33,480
Cause we are the fighters,
just fighting for

407
00:24:03,873 --> 00:24:04,703
Thank

408
00:24:04,786 --> 00:24:10,800
you.
